 ## Overview
-Ray-grid traversal computes the ordered sequence of grid cells (voxels) intersected by a ray, returning the cell indices along with entry and exit distances (or times) for each segment [S1, S2, unofficial][S5]. It solves the problem of efficiently identifying which volumetric data elements a ray passes through without performing expensive per-voxel bounding box intersection tests or fixed-distance sampling [S5][S7, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from [Direct volume ray casting](19-direct-volume-ray-casting.md) by providing the geometric traversal logic (the "where" and "when") rather than the shading/compositing logic (the "what"), and from [Acceleration](18-acceleration.md) by operating on uniform or structured grids rather than hierarchical spatial partitioning structures like octrees [S5].
