 ## Background
-The foundational algorithm for uniform grid ray traversal was introduced by J. Amanatides and A. Woo in "A Fast Voxel Traversal Algorithm for Ray Tracing," published in Eurographics '87 [S2, unofficial]. This algorithm, often referred to as the Amanatides-Woo algorithm or 3D DDA, revolutionized ray tracing by providing an efficient way to traverse voxel grids without per-voxel intersection tests [S2, S6, unofficial].
-
-Subsequent developments have extended this core logic to handle non-uniform grids [S1, unofficial], hierarchical structures like octrees and VDBs [S4, unofficial][S11][S16, unofficial], and GPU-optimized variants for coherent ray packets [S2, S3, unofficial]. The algorithm is widely used in real-time voxel rendering (e.g., Minecraft-style games) [S6, unofficial] and scientific visualization [S1, unofficial].
